## Starting point (read on `main`, `2faf472f`)

| Where | What exists | Relevance |
|---|---|---|
| `docs/measurements/nexus-catalog/*.http` (82 files) | one exchange per file: `#` header (`scenario`, `nexus: 3.98.1-01 COMMUNITY (...)`, `measured`, `account`, `redacted`), request line + `Host` + `Authorization: Basic <redacted>` (or none), blank line, status line + whitelisted headers, blank line, body (JSON verbatim, `<empty body>`, or `<HTML body omitted: N bytes, <title>...</title>>`). Name `<scenario>--<admin|pull|anon>.http`. LF endings (`.gitattributes`). | Already redacted by NX-03 (no credential, no token, no cookie, header whitelist, `uploaderIp` redacted). Hosts seen: `127.0.0.1` only, plus `bench-upstream.nexus-bench.svc.cluster.local:5000` in `remoteUrl` (the bench's own service, already in the versioned descriptor). Version: **3.98.1-01 COMMUNITY**, measured 2026-11-17. |
| `docs/measurements/2026-11-17-nexus-catalog.md:277-279` | "the script that produced them is not versioned (it reads the secrets)" | criterion 6 has nothing to start from |
| `internal/imagesearch/catalog_http_test.go`, `verdict_http_test.go`, `catalog_test.go` | hand-written `httptest` handlers; `TestCatalogHTTPPrefix` serves `docker-hosted/api` for prefix `docker-hosted` | C2 below |
| `internal/registrymgr/nexus_test.go`, `nexus_members_test.go`, `nexus_errors_test.go`, `nexus_hardening_test.go` | hand-written Nexus; `TestNexusMembersOtherStatusIsNotARefusal` pins 404 = failed discovery | C1 below |
| `internal/imagesearch/catalog.go:72-77` (R1) | prefix set and no name carries it → `ErrPrefixNotInCatalog` → `Classify` refused | criterion 3 |
| `internal/oci/catalog.go:32` | DevDesk always asks `/v2/_catalog?n=1000` | the NX-03 catalog files were recorded **without** `n`, except `page-group-n1000--admin` |
| `internal/ui/oci_resources/commands.go:376` (`registryAPIURL`) | keeps the path of the entry URL | an entry `http://127.0.0.1:30481/repository/docker-hosted` walks `/repository/docker-hosted/v2/_catalog` (measured 200) |
| `internal/ui/oci_resources/registry_browser.go:389` (`listsCacheOnly`) | `Cached only` is decided from the config, in the UI package | not reachable from `imagesearch`/`registrymgr` tests; needs NX-04 answers anyway |
| `internal/nexusbench/nexusapi.go:96-182` (`newClient`, `do`) | the only Basic sender of the bench (guard 3 of `guard_test.go`); `do` drops the body of a non-2xx answer | the recorder needs a body-keeping variant here |
| `internal/nexusbench/secrets.go:261` (`writeFileAtomic`), `cmd/nexus-bench/status.go:107-199` (dataset comparison) | reusable | recorder |
| `internal/nexusbench/descriptor.json` vs `testdata/descriptor.example.json` | identical today; only the first comes from an instance | Q3 |

### Contradictions between the measures and the existing tests (criterion 4)

- **C1 (registrymgr)** — see Q1. Not a wrong test: a wrong premise (D161's "403 for a pull
  account"). Resolution: Q1.
- **C2 (imagesearch, fixable here)** — `TestCatalogHTTPPrefix` and the prefix cases of
  `catalog_test.go:99-193` use a Nexus-shaped prefix (`docker-hosted`) with prefixed names,
  which Nexus 3.98.1 never returns. The filter they test is generic (a Harbor project or a
  GitLab group does prefix its names), so the test is kept and its data made neutral
  (`myproject/api`, prefix `myproject`), with a comment stating the measured Nexus fact and
  naming the fixture test. No behaviour change.
- **C3 (ui)** — see Q2.
- **No contradiction**: `TestCatalogHTTPRefusedAndEmpty` "prefix absent" (refused, now shown on a
  real catalog); `TestNexusRefusedMembersWithoutCredentialIsAnAnonymousRefusal` (403 anonymous,
  measured); "the generic endpoint carries no `memberNames`" (measured `"attributes": {}` for all
  three identities, so step 2 of `DetectGroup` is always reached).
- **Facts handed on, not decided here**: (F1) a proxy's `_catalog` lists `mirror/uncached`,
  which it does not hold (it relays the upstream): input for NX-04/NX-09, pinned by a fixture
  test as "the search shows it"; (F2) `cleanMemberAlias` gives both bench members the alias
  `docker` (`docker-hosted`, `docker-proxy`): two group members with the same label. Display
  only, keys are URL + prefix; flagged for the PM, not fixed here.

## Non-functional requirements

- **No bench in `mise run test`/`ci`** (criterion 5): fixtures are embedded files; the fake
  server is `httptest` on loopback; nothing reads `NEXUS_BENCH_*` or the secrets file.
- **No leak** (criterion 1): every fixture passes a leak check in `mise run test`; the recorder
  runs the same check, plus an exact search for the real passwords, before writing anything.
- **No hand-written answer can pass as measured**: a fixture is either byte-identical to its
  dated evidence under `docs/measurements/` or carries `# recorded-by: nexus-bench record`.
- **Recorder safety**: credentials only to the loopback origins of the descriptor, Basic only,
  GET only, a closed list of path shapes (no manifest, no blob: a read through the proxy caches,
  F9), no redirect followed, bodies bounded at 1 MiB, nothing written on any error, atomic
  writes, no secret in argv, output or file.
- **Load**: about 30 small files (a few hundred bytes each); test runtime well under a second.
- **Exploitability**: one command regenerates (`mise run nexus-bench:record`), refuses on a
  drifted bench with the command to run (`nexus-bench:reset`), and writes nothing for an answer
  that did not change apart from its date.

## Options

### Where the fixtures live

| Option | For | Against |
|---|---|---|
| A. Tests read `docs/measurements/nexus-catalog/` directly | one copy | regeneration would overwrite dated evidence of a measurement note; tests depend on a docs path; no `embed` (outside the module package tree) |

package fakenexus_test

import (
	"bytes"
	"fmt"
	"io"
	"net/http"
	"net/url"
	"strconv"
	"strings"
	"sync"
	"testing"

	"github.com/anthnel/devdesk/internal/nexusfixture"
	"github.com/anthnel/devdesk/internal/nexusfixture/fakenexus"
)

const (
	hostHTTP  = "127.0.0.1:30481" // the HTTP port: REST API and /repository/<name>
	hostGroup = "127.0.0.1:30482" // the group's Docker connector

	groupREST = "/service/rest/v1/repositories/docker/group/docker-group"
)

// recorder stands in for the *testing.T handed to fakenexus.New, so that a test
// can observe the error the server reports for an unrecorded request without
// failing itself. Everything else (Cleanup, Helper, Logf) goes to the real T.
// The server answers from another goroutine, hence the mutex.
type recorder struct {
	testing.TB
	mu   sync.Mutex
	errs []string
}

func (r *recorder) record(args ...any) {
	r.mu.Lock()
	defer r.mu.Unlock()
	r.errs = append(r.errs, strings.TrimSpace(fmt.Sprint(args...)))
}

func (r *recorder) Errorf(format string, args ...any) { r.record(fmt.Sprintf(format, args...)) }
func (r *recorder) Error(args ...any)                 { r.record(args...) }
func (r *recorder) Fatalf(format string, args ...any) { r.record(fmt.Sprintf(format, args...)) }
func (r *recorder) Fatal(args ...any)                 { r.record(args...) }

func (r *recorder) failures() []string {
	r.mu.Lock()
	defer r.mu.Unlock()
	return append([]string(nil), r.errs...)
}

// loadAll returns the embedded NX-03 campaign by name.
func loadAll(t *testing.T) map[string]nexusfixture.Fixture {
	t.Helper()
	fixtures, err := nexusfixture.Load("catalog")
	if err != nil {
		t.Fatalf("Load(catalog): %v", err)
	}
	if len(fixtures) == 0 {
		t.Fatal("the catalog campaign is empty")
	}
	byName := make(map[string]nexusfixture.Fixture, len(fixtures))
	for _, f := range fixtures {
		byName[f.Name] = f
	}
	return byName
}

func all(t *testing.T) []nexusfixture.Fixture {
	t.Helper()
	fixtures, err := nexusfixture.Load("catalog")
	if err != nil {
		t.Fatalf("Load(catalog): %v", err)
	}
	return fixtures
}

// pick returns the named fixtures, failing on a name that does not exist.
func pick(t *testing.T, names ...string) []nexusfixture.Fixture {
	t.Helper()
	byName := loadAll(t)
	out := make([]nexusfixture.Fixture, 0, len(names))
	for _, n := range names {
		f, ok := byName[n]
		if !ok {
			t.Fatalf("no embedded fixture named %q", n)
		}
		out = append(out, f)
	}
	return out
}

// get sends GET target to base as the identity (no Authorization for anonymous)
// and returns the answer with its body read. Redirects are not followed.
func get(t *testing.T, base, target string, id nexusfixture.Identity) (*http.Response, []byte) {
	t.Helper()
	req, err := http.NewRequest(http.MethodGet, base+target, nil)
	if err != nil {
		t.Fatalf("NewRequest: %v", err)
	}
	if id != nexusfixture.Anonymous {
		req.SetBasicAuth(fakenexus.User(id), fakenexus.Password)
	}
	return do(t, req)
}

func do(t *testing.T, req *http.Request) (*http.Response, []byte) {
	t.Helper()
	client := &http.Client{
		Transport:     &http.Transport{DisableKeepAlives: true},
		CheckRedirect: func(*http.Request, []*http.Request) error { return http.ErrUseLastResponse },
	}
	resp, err := client.Do(req)
	if err != nil {
		t.Fatalf("%s %s: %v", req.Method, req.URL, err)
	}
	defer func() { _ = resp.Body.Close() }()
	body, err := io.ReadAll(resp.Body)
	if err != nil {
		t.Fatalf("reading %s %s: %v", req.Method, req.URL, err)
	}
	return resp, body
}

// repositories is the first (only) recorded body of a fixture.
func recordedBody(t *testing.T, f nexusfixture.Fixture) []byte {
	t.Helper()
	if len(f.Exchanges) == 0 {
		t.Fatalf("%s has no exchange", f.Name)
	}
	return f.Exchanges[0].Body
}

func TestCredentials(t *testing.T) {
	cases := []struct {
		id   nexusfixture.Identity
		want string
	}{
		{nexusfixture.Admin, "admin"},
		{nexusfixture.Pull, "bench-pull"},
		{nexusfixture.Anonymous, ""},
	}
	for _, c := range cases {
		if got := fakenexus.User(c.id); got != c.want {
			t.Errorf("User(%q) = %q, want %q", c.id, got, c.want)
		}
	}
	if fakenexus.Password == "" {
		t.Error("Password is empty")
	}
}

func TestOneServerPerRecordedHost(t *testing.T) {
	s := fakenexus.New(t, all(t)...)
	a, b := s.URL(hostHTTP), s.URL(hostGroup)
	if a == b {
		t.Fatalf("both hosts share one server: %s", a)
	}
	for _, raw := range []string{a, b} {
		u, err := url.Parse(raw)
		if err != nil {
			t.Fatalf("URL %q: %v", raw, err)
		}
		if u.Scheme != "http" || u.Hostname() != "127.0.0.1" || u.Port() == "" {
			t.Errorf("URL %q is not a loopback http://127.0.0.1:port address", raw)
		}
		if u.Path != "" {
			t.Errorf("URL %q carries a path", raw)
		}
	}
	if s.URL(hostHTTP) != a {
		t.Error("URL is not stable between calls")
	}
}

func TestEachHostServesOnlyItsOwnFixtures(t *testing.T) {
	s := fakenexus.New(t, all(t)...)

	// The same path is recorded on both hosts with different answers.
	resp, _ := get(t, s.URL(hostHTTP), "/v2/_catalog", nexusfixture.Anonymous)
	if resp.StatusCode != http.StatusNotFound {
		t.Errorf("HTTP port /v2/_catalog status = %d, want 404 (recorded: path routing, no shared catalog)", resp.StatusCode)
	}
	resp, _ = get(t, s.URL(hostGroup), "/v2/_catalog", nexusfixture.Anonymous)
	if resp.StatusCode != http.StatusOK {
		t.Errorf("group connector /v2/_catalog status = %d, want 200", resp.StatusCode)
	}

	// A path recorded on the HTTP port only is unknown on the connector.
	rec := &recorder{TB: t}
	s2 := fakenexus.New(rec, all(t)...)
	resp, _ = get(t, s2.URL(hostGroup), groupREST, nexusfixture.Admin)
	if resp.StatusCode != http.StatusNotImplemented {
		t.Errorf("REST path on the connector host: status = %d, want 501", resp.StatusCode)
	}
	if len(rec.failures()) != 1 {
		t.Errorf("REST path on the connector host: %d test errors, want 1: %q", len(rec.failures()), rec.failures())
	}
}

func TestIdentityPicksTheAnswer(t *testing.T) {
	byName := loadAll(t)
	s := fakenexus.New(t, all(t)...)

	cases := []struct {
		id      nexusfixture.Identity
		fixture string
		status  int
	}{
		{nexusfixture.Admin, "rest-repositories-group-docker-group--admin", http.StatusOK},
		{nexusfixture.Pull, "rest-repositories-group-docker-group--pull", http.StatusNotFound},
		{nexusfixture.Anonymous, "rest-repositories-group-docker-group--anon", http.StatusForbidden},
	}
	for _, c := range cases {
		t.Run(string(c.id), func(t *testing.T) {
			resp, body := get(t, s.URL(hostHTTP), groupREST, c.id)
			if resp.StatusCode != c.status {
				t.Fatalf("status = %d, want %d", resp.StatusCode, c.status)
			}
			if want := byName[c.fixture].Exchanges[0]; want.Stub == "" && !bytes.Equal(body, want.Body) {
				t.Errorf("body differs from the recorded one:\n got %q\nwant %q", body, want.Body)
			}
			if got := s.Hits(c.fixture); got != 1 {
				t.Errorf("Hits(%s) = %d, want 1", c.fixture, got)
			}
		})
	}

	// Only the admin answer lists the members.
	_, admin := get(t, s.URL(hostHTTP), groupREST, nexusfixture.Admin)
	if !bytes.Contains(admin, []byte(`"memberNames"`)) {
		t.Errorf("admin answer has no memberNames: %s", admin)
	}
	_, pull := get(t, s.URL(hostHTTP), groupREST, nexusfixture.Pull)
	if bytes.Contains(pull, []byte(`"memberNames"`)) {
		t.Errorf("pull answer lists members: %s", pull)
	}
}

func TestAnIdentityWithoutItsOwnFixtureIsNotServedAnother(t *testing.T) {
	// Only the admin answer is recorded here: neither anonymous nor the pull
	// account may be handed it.
	for _, id := range []nexusfixture.Identity{nexusfixture.Anonymous, nexusfixture.Pull} {
		t.Run(string(id), func(t *testing.T) {
			rec := &recorder{TB: t}
			s := fakenexus.New(rec, pick(t, "rest-repositories-group-docker-group--admin")...)
			resp, _ := get(t, s.URL(hostHTTP), groupREST, id)
			if resp.StatusCode != http.StatusNotImplemented {
				t.Errorf("status = %d, want 501", resp.StatusCode)
			}
			if n := len(rec.failures()); n != 1 {
				t.Errorf("%d test errors, want 1: %q", n, rec.failures())
			}
		})
	}
}

func TestUnrecordedRequestFailsTheTest(t *testing.T) {
	type req struct {
		name    string
		method  string
		target  string
		mutate  func(*http.Request)
		wantErr []string // substrings the error must carry
	}
	cases := []req{
		{
			name:    "wrong password",
			method:  http.MethodGet,
			target:  groupREST,
			mutate:  func(r *http.Request) { r.SetBasicAuth("admin", "not-the-password") },
			wantErr: []string{"no recorded answer"},
		},
		{
			name:    "unknown user",
			method:  http.MethodGet,
			target:  groupREST,
